WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:00.880
Welcome.

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:01.600
And that's it.

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:02.880
You're all set up.

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.480
Let me show you what you have now

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.560
and what you've chosen to leave for later.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.760
Basically, there are three separate things we're gonna look at.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.000
Here's a look at your AI's memory today.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.080
Now, your history was searchable the moment your

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.480
files were read in, and meaning search makes

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.160
it even better if you added it.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:19.840
Then there's your constitution.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.360
This shows how many of the questions

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.360
it answered, how many it only partly

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.600
answered, and which ones are still open.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.040
You can actually see your specific

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.880
numbers right beside the screen.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.640
If you notice some questions are still

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:32.560
open, that's not a problem at all.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.360
It just means your conversations so far didn't answer them.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.680
They're listed right at the end of your constitution,

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.240
under not yet known, so your AI knows to

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.920
ask you instead of trying to guess.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.600
Oh, and if your history happens to

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.360
be on an external drive, just keep

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.040
it plugged in when you need it.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.800
So how does it keep growing?

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.680
Well, when you ask, it reads more conversations, or your

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.160
new export, against the questions that are still open.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:55.040
It can also run on a

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:56.480
schedule, if you set one.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.800
And when you correct something, that specific

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.720
part of your constitution is rewritten.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:01.920
It never runs on its own

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.520
just because the setup is finished.

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:06.290
The suggested choice for a next step is to

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:09.570
ask one real example question, something like, How have

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:11.730
I approached this kind of decision before?

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:13.250
Take a look at the sources it brings

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.330
back and correct anything that doesn't fit.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:17.570
Or you can just say, Use my context.

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:19.810
From here on, your AI reads its memory at

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:21.810
the start of work, the way you do.

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:24.050
Try a question now or finish here?

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.810
Press a button below.
